## Usage

<Source
  language="typescript"
  dark
  code={`import { <%= className %> } from '@nuxeo-satori/platform/components';`}
/>

<Source
  language="html"
  dark
  code={`<nxs-<%= fileName %> [heading]="'acme.<%= propertyName %>.heading' | translate"<% if (isDocumentView) { %> [document]="document"<% } %> />`}
/>

Every input is optional. `heading` takes text you have already translated: the library ships no
translations for the text you give it. Used directly, it needs no providers.

### By registered ID

`provideNxsComponents()` registers it as `<%= componentId %>`. <%- host.placement %>

<Source language="json" dark code={`<%- placement %>`} />

## Where its data comes from

<%- host.data %> Anything more it needs comes through the platform's services, which carry the
application's sign-in, never `fetch()`.

## Examples

### Inside a section

Set `headingLevel` one below the heading of the section it sits in. The default is `2`.

<Canvas of={<%= storiesName %>.InsideASection} /><% if (isDocumentView) { %>

### Without a document

Until the host has a document to pass, only the heading renders.

<Canvas of={<%= storiesName %>.WithoutADocument} /><% } %>

## Accessibility

- **Heading.** The heading is a native heading element at `headingLevel`. Choose the level that
  fits the page outline. A blank heading renders no element, rather than an empty one.
- **Reading order.** Everything it shows is text, read in the order it appears. It has no role of
  its own.
- **Keyboard.** The component takes no focus.
